title: scene_marcin
---
<<bg shrine>>

Ariel didn’t have to walk for long, he quickly spotted a small chapel nearby.
Walking towards it he felt himself relaxing, he felt as if someone was slowly taking a huge rock out of his arms.
The young priest stopped in front of the chapel, looking around.
It was rather small, cozy, filled with small trinkets probably placed here by the followers that came here to talk to the Creator.
It made his heart lighter, his lips curled into a small smile and he placed his hands in front of his heart, wrapping his fingers together as he prepared himself for a prayer.
Talking with the Creator always helped Ariel clear his mind.

<<show ariel basic right>>

Ariel: I’m not sure if I'm ready.
Ariel: What if I fail?
Ariel: What if because of me this whole town will perish, consumed by sin?
Ariel: What if…

???: Fear not, for I am with you!

A loud voice pierced through Ariel’s voice, making him flinch. 

<<show marcin basic left>>

There was someone in front of him.
A big figure with wings and a halo above its head…
An…
Angel. 

// <<show marcin laugh left>>

Angel: Oh, sorry, I always wanted to say that.
Angel: Makes me sound all mighty and stuff you know? 

Ariel was stunned.
There was an angel right in front of him.
A real angel, the messenger of the Creator.

//<<show marcin basic left>>

Angel: Let’s start again, shall we?
Angel: I’m Marchain, the spirit guide sent to you from the Above by the Creator itself to help you with the task you’re about to face.

Marchain: And you..? 
-> I’m Father Ariel!
   Marchain: Oh, look at you so professional.
   Marchain: Relax!
   Marchain: Also, I already know who you are.
   Marchain: I'm just messing with you a little bit. 
-> You can call me your future husband.
   Marchain: Oh um…
   Marchain: Well, that's not… Anyway…
   Marchain: Back to the matter at hand.

Marchain: As I was saying.
Marchain: I've been sent to help you.
Marchain: The Creator heard your prayers, little priest.
Marchain: Your little heart is filled with so much doubt right now, we can’t have that here! 

An angel poked Ariel in the chest, making him blush a little bit.

// <<show ariel blush left>>

This is not how Ariel was picturing angels.
He saw them as mighty beings, powerful, serious, authoritative, but this?
This one was playful, cheerful and definitely not scary. 

// <<show ariel basic left>>

Ariel: The task I’m about to face…
Ariel: The corruption in the city.
Ariel: I’m.. not sure if I’m able to help. 

Marchain: I’ll be here to guide you, to listen to your doubts, to show you the right path when you're lost.
Marchain: I’ll be next to you to show you the way.
Marchain: That’s my duty, little priest.
Marchain: You just have to accept it.
Marchain: Open your heart for me.

Marchain: That’s all I’m asking for. 
-> If you’re already here, can’t you do it? Wouldn’t that be easier?
   Marchain: You’d think that makes more sense, and it probably does.
   Marchain: But I can only guide someone who’s been already chosen by the Creator.
   Marchain: Someone like you.  
-> I can also think of other ways that will help me.
   Marchain: You flatter me, but I don’t think that will really help you right now. 
-> I trust you… I’ll trust your guidance.
   Marchain: I won’t disappoint you little priest. I mean how could I, I’m a spirit guide.
   Marchain: It’s what I do. 
   Marchain: I’ll be right by your side when you need me.

// <<show marcin laugh left>>

Marchain: But now shoo, off you go.
Marchain: Go…
Marchain: Gather some information about the townsfolks or something. 
Marchain: And no more doubtful thoughts.
Marchain: Got it? 

It made Ariel laugh.

This whole conversation was so silly he already felt way better, and knowing that he’s under the spirit guide protection?
Now Ariel felt like he could do anything.

Ariel: Got it. 

Ariel turned around to leave the chapel. 

Ariel: Actually I have a que-! 

<<hide marcin>>

But when Ariel turned his head to look at the angel one more time, no one was there anymore.

Ariel: “I’ll be right by your side when you need me”.

Angels weren’t supposed to lie, were they?

<<hide ariel>>

But maybe it only works for serious situations.

Ariel decided to take Marchain’s advice to heart and go back to town.

Now that he knows what he’s going to face there, it should be a little bit easier.


<<jump scene_lilian>>

